---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const emailHref = `mailto:me@eirikbreen.com?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Platform / PCI Linux")}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Eirik Breen, systems consultant in Oslo. PCI DSS Linux, Kubernetes with GitOps, and payment HSMs at Orange Business."
>
  <article class="page about-page">
    <header class="intro">
      <p class="kicker">Systems consultant, Oslo</p>
      <h1>I run Linux platforms that have to pass an audit.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I design and run Kubernetes for enterprise customers at Orange Business. The PCI DSS Linux
        environments I look after have passed their security audits. I also lead a project running
        redundant payment HSMs across data centres.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="work-heading">
      <h2 id="work-heading">The work</h2>
      <p>
        The clusters are K3s and MKS, with GitOps through Argo CD, Cilium for networking, and secrets
        in OpenBao and Vault, on RHEL. Ansible and CI/CD carry the routine changes. Splunk and the
        Elastic Stack are how I find out what actually happened.
      </p>
      <p>
        A lot of it runs under PCI DSS, so "probably fine" is not a deployment strategy. For one
        customer I lead the HSM work, redundant Thales PayShield and Luna across data centres. I
        write changes so the next person can read them. A boring pipeline beats a clever one nobody
        can debug at three in the morning, and I do not merge automation that hides what it did.
      </p>
      <p>
        I came up through operations. Senior on the incident team at Orange Business before consulting,
        mostly RHEL and Azure, on a roster that covered nights and weekends. I mentored apprentices
        through their trade exam. Before that, first and second line at HDO in Gjøvik, supporting AMK
        centres, out-of-hours clinics, and A&amp;E on Norway's emergency network. Trade certificate
        with distinction. That is the origin, not the job I want next.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="after-heading">
      <h2 id="after-heading">After hours</h2>
      <p>
        The homelab runs K3s. Claude Code and OpenCode are in the day job.
        When something survives more than a weekend it lands with
        <a href="/projects">the other things I made</a>
        or <a href="/blog">on the blog</a>. One that shipped is PixelWitness, a browser extension that
        scores images for likely AI generation without sending them off the machine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Write me</h2>
      <p>Platform work, PCI Linux, GitOps, or payment HSMs are all worth an email.</p>
      <p class="cta">
        <a href={emailHref}>me@eirikbreen.com</a>
      </p>
      <p class="secondary">
        Dates, employers, and the full stack are on <a href="/resume">the CV</a>.
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/eirik-breen" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
        works if you prefer.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: min(100%, 38rem);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 18ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 5.8vw, 3.05rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.08;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 1.35rem 0 0;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 1.08rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5.5vw, 3.25rem);
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  section p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  section p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  section a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.28em;
  }

  section a:hover {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .contact {
    padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .cta a {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.8vw, 1.6rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .secondary {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
